            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Total daily energy expenditure (TDEE) is the total number of calories your body burns in 24 hours. It comprises BMR (60-75% of TDEE), TEF (10%), NEAT (15-30%), and EAT (5-10%). Knowing your TDEE is the first step to setting an accurate calorie deficit for fat loss."
            }
