            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How does metabolism change during fat loss?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "As you lose weight, your metabolism naturally slows because a smaller body requires fewer calories. This is called metabolic adaptation. Research shows that after significant weight loss, resting metabolic rate can drop 10-20% more than expected based on weight loss alone, which is why adjusting your intake periodically is essential."
            }
        },
